Operations' two additions are not implemented, because this node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`.

- **Log file:** there is no filesystem or WASI import in the world, so the node cannot write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the four-host allowlist, so the host would trap the request. It would also send the input text to a service the node was not granted. Either addition needs a separate grant in the graph.

The node below fetches each subscribed URL. A URL whose host is outside the allowlist is recorded as a failure instead of being requested, so one bad entry does not trap the whole tick.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
